				<r3d:description language="eng">OstData is a research data repository for East, Central and Southeast European Studies. OstData supports publishing research data on the region of Eastern, Central and Southeastern Europe. This covers the following countries: Albania, Bosnia-Herzegovina, Bulgaria, Estonia, Finland, Kosovo, Croatia, Latvia, Lithuania, Moldova, Montenegro, Modern Greece, North Macedonia, Poland, Romania, Russia, Serbia, Slovakia, Slovenia, Czechia, Ukraine, Hungary, Belarus, Cyprus (Greek).
Multi- and interdisciplinary research on Eastern, Central and Southeastern Europe is rooted in the historical, cultural and social sciences and encompasses the following academic approaches in particular: Archaeology, Ethnology/Anthropology, History, Political Science, Sociology, Linguistics and Literary Studies and Economics</r3d:description>
